AIterprise AIBOM Scanner (aiterprise-scan)
Copyright 2026 AIterprise

This product includes data derived from third-party sources, each under its own terms:

- OSV / OpenSSF malicious-packages records (data/ait/malicious-versions.json.gz) —
  https://osv.dev and https://github.com/ossf/malicious-packages. Each record carries
  its own terms. They are to be checked per record before redistribution; this build does not
  check them yet (docs/STATUS.md).
- OSV vulnerability records for AI packages (data/ait/vuln-subset.json.gz) — https://osv.dev.
  Each record keeps the licence of the database it came from (for example the GitHub Advisory
  Database and the PyPA Advisory Database, both CC-BY 4.0); the record ids identify the source.
- CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog (data/ait/kev.json) — public domain (CC0).
- Model and dataset licence verdicts (data/ait/licence-verdicts.json) are AIterprise
  summaries of the cited licence texts. They are advisory and are not legal advice.

First-party AIterprise data, Apache-2.0 like the code: data/ait/taxonomy.json,
data/ait/ai-assets.json (prompt file names, AI provider API hosts, vector-store images and calls),
data/ait/command-rules.json, data/ait/poison-patterns.json, data/ait/model-rules.json,
data/ait/popular-packages.json (package names only) and data/ait/rule-quality.json
(false-positive measurements, see tools/measure_fp.py).

No third-party source code is vendored in this repository. Ed25519 (RFC 8032) and the minisign
format are implemented from their specifications.
